=== attack audit — v4 vs heuristic on W0Base
  100 episodes, win_rate 0.940, 31.0 turns/ep

  attack rate                 1353/4486   0.302 [0.288,0.315]   creatures sent / could have attacked
  attack-optimality            791/1262   0.627 [0.600,0.653]   UPPER BOUND: includes no-choice combats
    ...where a choice existed   791/1262   0.627 [0.600,0.653]   the honest one
  attack-optimality (CA)       801/1262   0.635 [0.608,0.661]   reference charges for the crack-back

  score gap (myopic)         3753 over 1262 combats
  score gap (CA)             4134
  missed lethal              1   (own category, never a gap)
  errors UNDER / OVER        274 / 193   (sent fewer / more than ref)
  truncated subsets/replies  1 / 0
  combats with no choice     0   (MATCH there is the position's)

  cost: policy search 0 ms total, 0.00 ms/combat; audit 406410 ms (instrument, not play)
  nodes: 0k resolve() calls, 0 per combat

  READ WITH: the reference is one combat deep and prices at zero
  the fact that an attacker cannot block next turn, so it
  over-credits attacking. A rise in attack-optimality alongside
  a rise in attack rate is partly tautological; the CA row and
  the UNDER/OVER split are what separate them.
